# Markdown is not formatted. Two reasons:
# 1. Docs are prose with hand-tuned line wrapping; prettier pads tables to
#    full width, and any change to a single cell redraws the whole table.
# 2. `.claude/commands/opsx/*.md` are generated by `openspec update --force` — the formatter
#    would fight it on every package update.
**/*.md

# Golden and baseline — protected territory. The snapshot there is an artifact, and the test next to it is
# exactly the check that must not be weakened: `it.skip` silences it no less than editing the numbers.
# So neither the formatter nor an agent (PreToolUse hook) touches the directory, and any change
# to it goes in a separate commit prefixed `golden:`/`baseline:` (tests/README.md).
**/test/golden/**
**/sim/baseline/**

# `content/` is deliberately NOT ignored. A JSON Schema constrains shape, never indentation,
# key order or line endings, and these files are written by agents, not by a generator — in a
# directory designed for thousands of them (ADR 0003). Diff stability is exactly what the
# PR-2 review question depends on. Verified: the tree already matches prettier, so turning
# this on costs nothing and only locks it in.

node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml
